  ​The parades are over\, but the table&#x27\;s still set. Map The Room i
 s an intimate\, personalized dinner where your answers shape who you sit b
 eside\, how you’re introduced\, and the visual maps\, prompts\, and clue
 s created for the night. It makes the invisible visible: the patterns\, ov
 erlaps\, and quiet things people may have in common before conversation ev
 en begins. ​For one night\, the room shows you how differently\, and une
 xpectedly\, we may connect. ‍
