BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lives: Visible and Leftovers | Dykeumentary Night Screening
DTSTART:20260817T193000
DTEND:20260817T193000
UID:69f6238dd1aaee7f691d567e1ca060be@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:2\,000 photos hidden away for over fifty years reveal the rich
  history of Chicago’s working-class butch/fem life\, pre-Stonewall. Dyke
 umentary Night is a monthly lesbian movie night in Toronto\, hosted at Thr
 ee Dollar Bill. This month&#x27\;s movie is a short film double feature sh
 owcasing two films called &quot\;Lives: Visible&quot\; and &quot\;Leftover
 s.&quot\; SYNOPSIS LIVES: VISIBLE (2017\, 35 mins): Lesbians in a box… t
 wo thousand private snapshots hidden away for over fifty years reveal the 
 rich history of Chicago’s working class butch/fem life in the pre-Stonew
 all era. Spanning four decades\, from the 1930s to the early 1970s\, the s
 napshots provide a rare look at a vanished and vibrant Lesbian culture: im
 ages of lovers and friends as they played\, posed\, serially switched part
 ners\, worked\, partied\, drank\, and aged. Now we all take selfies\; thes
 e women used a Brownie camera to tell the story of their community. LIVES:
  VISIBLE explores the ephemeral nature of culture and the power of the ima
 ges we make. LEFTOVERS (2014\, 23 mins): Norma and Virginia were lovers fo
 r almost fifty years. They died isolated\; the vibrant pre-Stonewall lesbi
 an community of their youth long gone. A love story about the unforeseen t
 rajectory of lives lived outside the mainstream told through the 2000 snap
 shots left behind. ‍
LOCATION:Three Dollar Bill\, 1592 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/lives-visible-and-leftovers-dykeumentary-n
 ight-screening
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
